> Where the fill enters

For the original graph all105 natural-order fill edges enter at the first
elimination. Later elimination steps still perform clique pair trials on the
dense remaining graph even when no new edge is inserted. The next figure
separates observed pair trials from actual new edges. These counts explain work
more precisely than calling all neighbor pairs fill.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/degree_steps.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/minimum_degree.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::elimination_trace(dm::algorithms::minimum_degree_arrow(),
                                          dm::algorithms::elimination_natural_order(16));
    std::vector<double> x, trials, fill;
    std::print("| step | eliminated | live degree | pair trials | new fill |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k < t.steps.size(); ++k) {
        auto &s = t.steps[k];
        auto d = s.neighbors.size();
        auto pairs = d ? d * (d - 1) / 2 : 0;
        x.push_back(k);
        trials.push_back(pairs);
        fill.push_back(s.fill.size());
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", k, s.vertex, d, pairs,
                   s.fill.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, trials, "actual pair trials", {37, 99, 235}, 6).points(
        x, fill, "actual new edges", {220, 38, 38}, 6).title(
        "Original natural elimination: pair trials versus new fill").x_label(
        "elimination step").y_label("undirected pairs").save_svg(
        "build/degree_steps.svg");
}
```
